// Machine-specific Claude Code settings.
// Merged into ~/.claude/settings.json by chezmoi at apply time. This is chezmoi's own
// overlay file; Claude Code itself does not read a user-level settings.local.json.
// For the exact merge rules, see `merge()` in the script that generates settings.json:
//   chezmoi source-path ~/.claude/settings.json
//
// In short: only whole-line // comments like these are allowed (no trailing comments);
// nested objects merge recursively; lists (e.g. permissions.allow) are unioned with the
// committed list, so entries here can only add to it; scalars are replaced. A broken file
// aborts `chezmoi apply` (and `diff`/`status`) with an error naming this file rather than
// dropping settings.
// After editing, run `chezmoi apply` to regenerate ~/.claude/settings.json.
